# Phase 3 remoting transport — execution log (20260927T003044Z)

## Scope and decision
- Continued Java 5.5.1 exception-path audit using `NettyRemotingAbstract.invoke0`, its `writeAndFlush(...).addListener` failure branch, and `requestFail`.
- Confirmed asynchronous socket write failures are reported by Java as `RemotingSendRequestException(remoteAddress, null)`: failed channel future calls `requestFail`, sets send status false without assigning a cause, then callback construction includes channel remote address and null cause.
- Mapped Rust `TransportError::Send` / `Closed` returned from the asynchronous write to `SendRequest { remote_addr, cause: None }`; preserved `Timeout` unchanged. Then confirmed command encoding occurs after Java's pending-response registration and inside its Netty outbound write pipeline, so local frame-encoding errors at that point also fail through `requestFail`; Rust now maps that post-registration `Codec` error to the same send-request category. Queue admission timeout remains timeout.
- Extended `asynchronous_write_failure_matches_java_request_fail_classification` to cover codec/frame-size failures as well.
- Updated compatibility inventory and callback/error taxonomy notes. Broader admission/connect/shutdown taxonomy remains PARTIAL pending further Java branch-by-branch audit.

